<h1>Policy Premium Summary</h1>

<p>
    The Policy Premium Summary provides a comprehensive report of active policies, total premium, and average premium calculations for the last 12 months. Use it to analyze premium trends, track client portfolios, or generate reports for management.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Policy Premium Summary report showing: summary cards with active policies count, total premium, and average premium, plus a data grid with client-by-client breakdown. Show the toggle for "Show all clients" and the CSV download button. -->

<h2>What the Policy Premium Summary Does</h2>

<p>
    This utility provides:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Active policy count</strong> – Number of policies that were active at any time in the last 12 months</li>
    <li><strong>Total premium</strong> – Sum of all premiums for active policies</li>
    <li><strong>Average premium</strong> – Average premium per policy</li>
    <li><strong>Client breakdown</strong> – Premium statistics organized by client</li>
    <li><strong>CSV export</strong> – Download data for further analysis in Excel or other tools</li>
    <li><strong>Flexible scope</strong> – View data for a single client or your entire book of business</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Visual diagram showing what the summary calculates: policies active in last 12 months → total premium → average premium. Show the data flow and calculations with icons. -->

<h2>Using the Policy Premium Summary</h2>

<p>
    To generate a premium summary:
</p>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Open the utility</strong> – Access the Policy Premium Summary from the Utilities menu or from a client record</li>
    <li><strong>Select scope</strong> – Choose whether to view:
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Single client</strong> – Premium data for one specific client (if opened from a client record)</li>
            <li><strong>All clients</strong> – Premium data for your entire book of business</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Toggle view</strong> – Use the "Show all clients" toggle to switch between single client and book-wide views</li>
    <li><strong>Review summary cards</strong> – See the high-level statistics:
        <ul>
            <li>Active Policies (12 months)</li>
            <li>Total Premium</li>
            <li>Average Premium per Policy</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Review client details</strong> – Scroll through the data grid to see client-by-client breakdown</li>
    <li><strong>Export if needed</strong> – Click "Download CSV" to export the data for further analysis</li>
</ol>

