<h2>Exporting to CSV</h2>

<p>
    The CSV export feature allows you to:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Download raw data</strong> – Get all the data in a spreadsheet-friendly format</li>
    <li><strong>Further analysis</strong> – Import into Excel or other tools for custom analysis</li>
    <li><strong>Create reports</strong> – Use the data to build custom reports or presentations</li>
    <li><strong>Share data</strong> – Send premium data to management or accounting</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The CSV file includes all columns from the data grid:
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Client ID</li>
    <li>Client Name</li>
    <li>Lookup Code</li>
    <li>Active Policies Count</li>
    <li>Total Premium</li>
    <li>Average Premium</li>
</ul>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the CSV download button and a preview of the downloaded CSV file opened in Excel. Show the column headers and sample data. -->

<h2>Understanding the 12-Month Window</h2>

<p>
    The report analyzes policies that were active at any time during the last 12 months:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Policies that started</strong> – Policies that became effective within the last 12 months</li>
    <li><strong>Policies that ended</strong> – Policies that expired within the last 12 months</li>
    <li><strong>Currently active policies</strong> – Policies that are active now</li>
    <li><strong>Historical policies</strong> – Policies that were active during the period but have since expired</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The status message shows the start date of the 12-month window, so you know exactly what period is being analyzed.
</p>

